-- title:
--   The injective factor of an operator has no larger norm
-- statement:
--   Let $j:Z\to X$ be a bounded operator between real normed spaces, and let $\tilde j:Z/\ker j\to X$ be the induced injective operator, $\tilde j([z])=j(z)$, where the quotient carries the quotient norm. Then
--   $$
--   \|\tilde j\|\le\|j\| .
--   $$
--
--   Factoring out the kernel does not increase the operator norm.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/CompactQuotient.lean#L40-L54

